  "reply_text": "Found one merge-blocking bug:\n\n**[P1] `topTags` mutates the input, breaking the sidebar’s recent strip** — `src/tags.js:10`  \n`tags.sort(...)` reorders the caller’s array in place. Since `sidebar()` builds the cloud before reading `tags.slice(0, 5)`, “recent” shows the highest-count tags instead of the first tags in the original order. This also violates the README’s non-mutation guarantee.\n\nReproduced with tags `first:1, second:9, third:4`:\n- Expected recent: `first, second, third`\n- Actual recent: `second, third, first`\n\n**Suggested fix:** sort a copy (`[...tags].sort(...)`) and add regression tests asserting that the input stays unchanged and the sidebar preserves recent order.\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but none checks this behavior. No files changed.",
